sentences.l:
for very much in due order the Achaeans' fate you sing,
all that they did and suffered and all that they toiled through, the Achaeans,
as if perhaps either yourself being present or from another having heard.

if indeed these things to me according to what is fitting you recount,
at once I to all men will tell,
that, then, to you a ready-minded god granted god-spoken song.”

And as a woman weeps, having flung herself about her dear husband,
who before his own city and his people has fallen,
for the town and his children warding-off the pitiless day;

and they, behind,
striking with spears her back and also her shoulders,
lead her up into slavery, to have toil and misery;

From when we dine, and stirred, the divine minstrel,
from then not yet has ceased from woeful lament
the stranger;

sentences.t:
ἦ τίς τοι καὶ πηὸς ἀπέφθιτο Ἰλιόθι πρὸ
ἐσθλὸς ἐών, γαμβρὸς ἢ πενθερός, οἵ τε μάλιστα
κήδιστοι τελέθουσι μεθ’ αἷμά τε καὶ γένος αὐτῶν;
